  4  One watcher thread polls /api/play/status like the Telegram bot (3/10/30 s by age, at most 50 invoices). queued ->
     "Zapped and queued, you are #N"; expired -> a short note; paid-but-not-queued -> the station is told through the
     admin-notes channel (the Telegram bot relays it to SF) and the listener is told the station knows.
  4b When a paid song is NOW PLAYING, the bot quotes the listener's own "play" note (NIP-18 q tag + nostr:note1…) in
     SF's words: "Now playing on NoderunnersRadio.com🎧 Artist — Title." Once per song, kept on disk from queued to air.
  5  Limits: 60-char queries, 20 s between searches per person, 40 replies per hour station-wide (then it goes quiet and
     tells SF once), the announcer's blocklist on the echoed query (a blocked query is answered without the echo).
  6  DRY unless HOME/jukebox.LIVE exists: it reads and logs "[dry] would ..." and never mints or posts. HOME/jukebox.OFF
     makes it idle. Keys: HOME/nostr.env (nr-nostr-keys.py). Nothing else is written outside HOME/jukebox-state.json.

nr-nostr-jukebox              run (the service)        nr-nostr-jukebox --check     what it would do, no side effects
nr-nostr-jukebox --selftest   offline tests: a fake relay and a fake station on the loopback, nothing leaves the box
